{
  "id": "adjektive-nach-sein",
  "name": "Adjectives: agreement and position",
  "level": "A1",
  "status": "entwurf",
  "variety": "it-IT",
  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "subtitle": "An adjective matches its noun: masculine or feminine, one or more. It usually comes after the noun: una casa bianca, i libri nuovi.",
  "briefMarks": ["-o", "-a", "-i", "-e"],
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "article", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun" },
      { "text": "adjective", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">un</span> appartamento <span class=\"vp-verb\">piccolo</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">una</span> casa <span class=\"vp-verb\">piccola</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">gli</span> appartamenti <span class=\"vp-verb\">piccoli</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">le</span> case <span class=\"vp-verb\">piccole</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Adjectives in <strong>-o</strong> have four forms: <em>alto, alta, alti, alte</em>. <em>Marco è alto. Giulia è alta.</em>",
        "tag": "Four forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "Adjectives in <strong>-e</strong> have two forms: one for masculine and feminine, and a plural in <strong>-i</strong>: <em>un appartamento grande, una casa grande, le case grandi</em>; <em>un vicino gentile, le vicine gentili</em>.",
        "tag": "Two forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "Nationalities follow the same rules and take a small letter: <em>italiano, italiana, italiani, italiane</em>; <em>cinese, cinesi</em>; <em>inglese, inglesi</em>. <em>Sono italiana.</em>",
        "tag": "Nationalities"
      },
      {
        "html": "The adjective usually comes <strong>after</strong> the noun: <em>una macchina rossa, un ristorante cinese</em>. Colours and nationalities always come after. A few very common ones can also come first: <em>una bella casa, un piccolo problema</em>.",
        "tag": "Position"
      },
      {
        "html": "After <em>essere</em>, the adjective still matches the subject: <em>La strada è tranquilla. I bambini sono stanchi.</em>",
        "tag": "After essere"
      },
      {
        "html": "A group of men and women takes the masculine plural: <em>Marco e Giulia sono stanchi.</em>",
        "tag": "Mixed group"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>la casa bianco</em> → ✓ <em>la casa bianca</em>. ✗ <em>gli appartamenti caro</em> → ✓ <em>gli appartamenti cari</em>. ✗ <em>una rossa macchina</em> → ✓ <em>una macchina rossa</em>. ✗ <em>Sono Italiano</em> → ✓ <em>Sono italiano</em>. The short forms <em>bel, buon</em> (<em>un bel posto</em>) come at B1. Revise <a href=\"/plurals\">Plurals</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "The forms of an adjective",
          "head": ["Type", "masc. sing.", "fem. sing.", "masc. pl.", "fem. pl."],
          "rows": [
            ["-o", "alto", "alta", "alti", "alte"],
            ["-e", "grande", "grande", "grandi", "grandi"],
            ["nationality in -o", "italiano", "italiana", "italiani", "italiane"],
            ["nationality in -e", "cinese", "cinese", "cinesi", "cinesi"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Useful adjectives",
          "head": ["Adjective", "Opposite", "Meaning"],
          "rows": [
            ["grande", "piccolo", "big, small"],
            ["nuovo", "vecchio", "new, old"],
            ["caro", "economico", "expensive, cheap"],
            ["facile", "difficile", "easy, difficult"],
            ["pulito", "sporco", "clean, dirty"],
            ["alto", "basso", "tall, short"]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "boxes": [
        {
          "badge": "Careful: colours",
          "variant": "dat",
          "items": [
            "Colours in -o have four forms: il libro bianco, la casa bianca.",
            "Colours in -e have two: la porta verde, le porte verdi.",
            "blu, rosa and viola never change: la macchina blu, le macchine blu."
          ]
        },
        {
          "badge": "Careful: -co, -ca, -go, -ga",
          "items": [
            "bianco → bianchi, bianca → bianche. stanco → stanchi.",
            "lungo → lunghi, lunga → lunghe.",
            "But: simpatico → simpatici (simpatica → simpatiche)."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
